NAME
       mkstemp, mkdtemp, tmpfile, remove - temporary files

SYNOPSIS
       #include <stdlib.h>
       #include <stdio.h>

       int   mkstemp(char *template);
       char *mkdtemp(char *template);
       FILE *tmpfile(void);
       char *tmpnam(char *s);
       int   remove(const char *path);

DESCRIPTION
       mkstemp replaces the trailing XXXXXX of TEMPLATE with unique
       characters, creates the file and returns it open. mkdtemp does
       the same for a directory.

       tmpfile returns a stream that disappears when closed. remove
       deletes a file or an empty directory.

       Prefer mkstemp over tmpnam: tmpnam only produces a name, and
       something else may create it before you do.

RETURN VALUE
       A descriptor, a pointer, or -1 or NULL with errno set.

SEE ALSO
       open(2), unlink(2), stdio(3)
